Subject: [PATCH] fs/dax: check zero/empty entry before dax_to_folio in
 dax_disassociate_entry

dax_disassociate_entry() derives the folio BEFORE testing whether the entry is
a zero/empty entry:

    struct folio *folio = dax_to_folio(entry);
    if (dax_is_zero_entry(entry) || dax_is_empty_entry(entry))
            return;
    dax_folio_put(folio);

For a zero/empty entry the encoded pfn is 0, so dax_to_folio() evaluates
page_folio(pfn_to_page(0)), which dereferences vmemmap[0]. On arches whose
system RAM does not start at pfn 0 (riscv places RAM at 0x40000000), vmemmap[0]
is not populated, so the dereference takes a load page fault. This is hit on
the very first DAX write fault that replaces a zero page:

  Unable to handle kernel paging request at ff1c000000000008
  epc: dax_to_folio+0x4a  ra: dax_disassociate_entry+0x16
   dax_iomap_pte_fault -> dax_insert_entry -> dax_disassociate_entry -> dax_to_folio
  Kernel panic - Attempted to kill init!  (booting with root=/dev/pmem0 rootflags=dax)

x86 never faults because pfn 0 has a struct page there, which is why the bug is
latent upstream but fatal for riscv fsdax (e.g. a DAX root filesystem).

Fix: move the zero/empty test ahead of dax_to_folio(), matching the ordering
already used by the other dax entry helpers. The folio is only needed on the
non-special path.

Out-of-tree note: the guest kernel (Linux v7.2) is external to this repo and is
built via `make guest-kernel KERNEL_SRC=<tree>`. Apply before building:

    patch -p1 -d "$KERNEL_SRC" < configs/patches/riscv64-dax-zeropage-folio.patch

Drop once the reorder lands upstream.

--- a/fs/dax.c
+++ b/fs/dax.c
@@ -505,11 +505,21 @@
 static void dax_disassociate_entry(void *entry, struct address_space *mapping,
 				bool trunc)
 {
-	struct folio *folio = dax_to_folio(entry);
+	struct folio *folio;
 
+	/*
+	 * Test for the zero/empty entry BEFORE deriving a folio. Their pfn is 0,
+	 * and dax_to_folio() -> page_folio(pfn_to_page(0)) dereferences
+	 * vmemmap[0], which is unmapped on arches whose RAM does not start at
+	 * pfn 0 (e.g. riscv, RAM at 0x40000000). Computing the folio first thus
+	 * faults in the DAX path (dax_iomap_pte_fault -> dax_insert_entry ->
+	 * here) when replacing a zero page. The unused-args warning for
+	 * mapping/trunc is pre-existing.
+	 */
 	if (dax_is_zero_entry(entry) || dax_is_empty_entry(entry))
 		return;
 
+	folio = dax_to_folio(entry);
 	dax_folio_put(folio);
 }
 
